# Build context filter for the evio_ejfat_replay image.
#
# Only cpp/ is COPYed into the build, so most of this is about keeping the
# context small and keeping captures, credentials and local artifacts out of
# the daemon entirely.
#
# Rule order matters: the last pattern that matches a path decides. The three
# sections below are (1) broad excludes, (2) re-include the C++ tree the build
# needs, (3) hard excludes that must win even inside cpp/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Broad excludes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control and repository metadata
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.gitmodules
.github

# Build directories and generated products
build/
**/build/
cmake-build-*/
**/CMakeFiles
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CTestTestfile.cmake
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/compile_commands.json
**/Testing
out/
dist/

# Java / Gradle half of the repository -- not part of the C++ image
.gradle/
gradle/
gradlew
gradlew.bat
build.gradle
settings.gradle
libs/
src/

# Editor, IDE and OS artifacts
.idea/
.vscode/
.cache/
.claude/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs, scratch space and documents
**/*.log
logs/
tmp/
scratch/
**/*.pdf

# Container files themselves (the Dockerfile is read out of band)
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
DOCKER.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Re-include the C++ tree -- the only thing the image build consumes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!cpp/
!cpp/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Things inside cpp/ that the build never reads
#
# `COPY cpp/ ./cpp/` sits above the CMake configure step, which costs ~6
# minutes: pkg_check_modules(e2sar) makes 19 pkg-config queries and each one
# re-walks gRPC's 206-file, 1214-edge .pc graph. Anything left in the context
# therefore buys a six-minute rebuild every time it is edited, so the prose and
# the host-side test script are kept out. CMake reads none of them -- only
# CMakeLists.txt, include/, src/ and tests/*.cpp|hpp.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cpp/*.md
cpp/**/*.md
cpp/tests/docker_smoke_test.sh
cpp/src/actor/services.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Hard excludes -- these win everywhere, cpp/ included
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Large EVIO captures and packet dumps: never baked into an image
data/
captures/
**/*.bin
**/*.evio
**/*.pcap
**/*.pcapng
**/*.dat

# Compiled objects and libraries that may be lying around in the tree
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dylib
**/*.dSYM
**/*.jar
**/*.class

# Credentials and site configuration
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
secrets/
**/credentials*
**/*token*
**/*secret*
